content.text:
The classic-view return is committed to `jusprin-newui` as a single commit, `bef30d0539` ("Offer a way back to the JusPrin view from classic view"). This was my first commit for this change, so there was nothing to squash. It isn't pushed.

**Other work left out of the commit:** this checkout also has uncommitted changes from other work. Some sat in the same files and functions I changed, so I staged only my own lines and left the rest uncommitted:
- the Tab handler for the Prepare canvas;
- File > Recent files handling;
- the overflow menu's project rows;
- the harness checks for those.

That work is still active: `HeaderControls` changed while I was committing.

**Not tested:** the commit by itself was never built. The app you tested was built from my changes plus that other work. I checked that nothing in the commit refers to any of the left-out code, but building the commit alone would mean a separate build tree, which takes about 40 minutes. The other work's own Tab checks were also cut from my harness functions. When that work is committed, it needs to put them back.
